Use umask 022 for the config.status temporary directory.

The upstream autoconf-generated bootstrap creates its temporary
directory with umask 077.  On HMDFS-backed CI workers every directory
inherits the setgid bit from the parent, which combines with umask 077
into group-unwritable directories that break subsequent config.status
runs ("Something went wrong bootstrapping makefile fragments").
Relaxing to umask 022 matches what the a52dec 0.7.4 recipe already
ships for the same worker quirk; mktemp-created directories are still
private to their owner.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -15850,12 +15850,12 @@
 # Create a (secure) tmp directory for tmp files.
 
 {
-  tmp=`(umask 077 && mktemp -d "./confXXXXXX") 2>/dev/null` &&
+  tmp=`(umask 022 && mktemp -d "./confXXXXXX") 2>/dev/null` &&
   test -d "$tmp"
 }  ||
 {
   tmp=./conf$$-$RANDOM
-  (umask 077 && mkdir "$tmp")
+  (umask 022 && mkdir "$tmp")
 } || as_fn_error $? "cannot create a temporary directory in ." "$LINENO" 5
 ac_tmp=$tmp
 
